IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `au-part5-readings`

-- Tests for the rules of reading in Part 5 (ss 12, 15A, 15AA, 15AB(2)(3), 15AC, 15AD, 15B(3)(3A)(4)(b), 16 to 18A, 18B(4)-(6),
-- 20, 21, 23). Expected values are written from the text. A gate that does not open returns NOTHING, and is asserted.

§ `Section 12`

-- "Every section of an Act shall have effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words."
#ASSERT `has effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a section of an Act: the section says nothing.
#ASSERT `has effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 15A`

-- An enactment that would not have been construed as exceeding the power is read subject to the Constitution and is valid.
#ASSERT `section 15A treats the enactment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `read and construed subject to the Constitution, and valid`
-- One that would have been construed as in excess is nevertheless valid to the extent to which it is not in excess.
#ASSERT `section 15A treats the enactment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `valid to the extent to which it is not in excess of the legislative power of the Commonwealth`
-- Not an enactment of an Act (for example an instrument): s 15A does not speak of it.
#ASSERT `section 15A treats the enactment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 15A treats the enactment` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 15AA`

`candidate one` MEANS `A candidate interpretation` OF "the first reading", TRUE, TRUE
`candidate two` MEANS `A candidate interpretation` OF "the second reading", FALSE, TRUE
`candidate three` MEANS `A candidate interpretation` OF "the third reading", TRUE, FALSE
`candidate four` MEANS `A candidate interpretation` OF "the fourth reading", FALSE, FALSE
`candidate one with the purpose unstated` MEANS `A candidate interpretation` OF "the first reading", TRUE, FALSE

-- Exactly one reading best achieves the purpose or object: it is the one preferred over each other.
#ASSERT `the interpretation to be preferred` (LIST `candidate one`, `candidate two`) EQUALS JUST `candidate one`
#ASSERT `the interpretation to be preferred` (LIST `candidate two`, `candidate three`) EQUALS JUST `candidate three`
-- "whether or not that purpose or object is expressly stated in the Act": the answer is the same.
#ASSERT `the interpretation to be preferred` (LIST `candidate one with the purpose unstated`, `candidate four`) EQUALS JUST `candidate one with the purpose unstated`
-- Two readings that both best achieve it: the section prefers "the" best reading and does not choose between equals (fork F20).
#ASSERT `the interpretation to be preferred` (LIST `candidate one`, `candidate three`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- None does: nothing is preferred.
#ASSERT `the interpretation to be preferred` (LIST `candidate two`, `candidate four`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the interpretation to be preferred` EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING

