§ `Section 15AC`

-- Same idea in a clearer style: the ideas are not taken to be different merely because the words differ.
#ASSERT `the ideas are taken to be different merely because different forms of words were used` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Without the earlier Act's idea, or without the clearer-style purpose, the section does not speak.
#ASSERT `the ideas are taken to be different merely because different forms of words were used` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the ideas are taken to be different merely because different forms of words were used` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the ideas are taken to be different merely because different forms of words were used` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 15AD`

#ASSERT `the example is exhaustive` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the example may extend the operation of the provision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No example in the Act: nothing is said.
#ASSERT `the example is exhaustive` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the example may extend the operation of the provision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 15B(3), (3A) and (4)(b)`

#ASSERT `an Act in force in an external Territory is taken to have effect in its coastal sea as if it were part of the Territory` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`an Act in force in an external Territory is taken to have effect in its coastal sea as if it were part of the Territory` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`an Act in force in an external Territory is taken to have effect in its coastal sea as if it were part of the Territory` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the reference to the external Territories is taken to include the coastal sea` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the reference to the external Territories is taken to include the coastal sea` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the reference to the external Territories is taken to include the coastal sea` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `is in the coastal sea of an external Territory` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `is in the coastal sea of an external Territory` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`is in the coastal sea of an external Territory` FALSE FALSE)

§ `Section 16`

#ASSERT `a reference in an Act is construed as a reference to` `a reference to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of the Act` EQUALS JUST `the Sovereign for the time being`
#ASSERT `a reference in an Act is construed as a reference to` `a reference to the Crown` EQUALS JUST `the Sovereign for the time being`
#ASSERT `a reference in an Act is construed as a reference to` `a reference to anyone else` EQUALS NOTHING

