-- Not an office established by an Act with a deputy chair title.
#ASSERT NOT (`the person may be referred to by this deputy chair title` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- The four deputy chair titles of (4).
#ASSERT `Deputy Chair` EQUALS `Deputy Chair`
#ASSERT NOT (`Deputy Chairwoman` EQUALS `Deputy Chairman`)

§ `Section 20`

#ASSERT `a reference to the holder or occupier includes the person` `holds or occupies it for the time being` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to the holder or occupier includes the person` `performs its duties for the time being` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-29: was ``a reference to the holder or occupier includes the person` `neither holds nor occupies it nor performs its duties` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the rule that JUST FALSE needs the text's own words (NOTES, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING") applies, and section 20 says a reference to the holder or occupier "includes" the two groups, an open list, so the answer is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `a reference to the holder or occupier includes the person` `neither holds nor occupies it nor performs its duties` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not a provision of an Act or Commonwealth agreement, or not a reference in general terms: s 20 does not speak.
#ASSERT `a reference to the holder or occupier includes the person` `holds or occupies it for the time being` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a reference to the holder or occupier includes the person` `holds or occupies it for the time being` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

